1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,800
Every software team has faced this crisis: a runtime exception strikes production, causing silent corruption and broken transactions. Standard AI coding assistants jump straight to rewriting entire files, hallucinating unseen APIs and introducing fatal regressions. Today, we need a smarter, safer way to debug Python.

2
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:46,799
Meet Sunny DevFix: an autonomous, causal Python debugging agent purpose-built for the Nebius and NVIDIA Hackathon. Re-architected with a professional developer workspace, Sunny DevFix pairs NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory with local deterministic AST guardrails, a cryptographic human approval barrier, and isolated container verification.

3
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:10,799
Let's inspect a live billing failure. In the workspace panel, we load a defective source file with a subtle typo in a billing calculation, alongside its raw traceback. Notice the Live Code Guardian beneath the editor: it performs real-time AST linting as you type. It flags unmapped identifiers immediately, without executing untrusted code.

4
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:35,799
Now, we engage the autonomous repair engine. With one click, Sunny DevFix dispatches the problem context to NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory. The agent state machine advances in real time: analyzing the traceback, mapping deepest call frames, and synthesizing a pinpoint repair. The causal engine explains exactly why the failure occurred.

5
00:01:36,000 --> 00:02:00,799
Before a single byte touches disk, Sunny DevFix requires explicit human authorization. The diff studio presents an exact side-by-side comparison and color-coded unified diff. Only the defective variable is corrected, preserving existing syntax. A one-time cryptographic approval token ensures no autonomous agent writes to your workspace without your consent.

6
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:21,800
Once approved, the patch is verified in an isolated Docker sandbox with zero network access, read-only filesystem, and memory limits. Exit codes and stdout are verified before and after. If anything is unexpected, our instant rollback token restores the exact pre-patch code in milliseconds.

7
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:39,800
Sunny DevFix is thoroughly verified. Our comprehensive test suite covers eighty passing unit and integration tests in under one second, with a median benchmark latency of zero point one eight milliseconds. A self-contained test bundle is ready for evaluator testing.

8
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:49,800
